@@@ meta
id: ARR-H-10
topic: Arrays
difficulty: Hard
type: FIND_THE_BUG
title: Pre-Trigger Snapshot From a Circular Sample Buffer
tags: embedded, circular-buffer, negative-modulo, data-logger, array-bounds, wraparound
@@@ statement_md
A crash data recorder samples a sensor continuously into a **circular buffer of 32 samples**. When a trigger fires (e.g. airbag deployment), it must freeze the last `P` samples **up to and including the trigger sample**, oldest first, so that engineers can see what happened just before the event. If fewer than `P` samples have been recorded since power-up, it freezes all of them.

The code works on the bench for the first trigger. In vehicle tests, some later triggers deliver garbage or crash the logger task, depending on **when** the trigger arrives relative to the buffer wrap-around. Under the judge, those cases are reported as an out-of-bounds access.

Find and fix the bug. Do not change the input or output format.

**Input**
- Line 1: `P n`, the pre-trigger length and the number of samples.
- Line 2: the `n` samples in time order.
- Line 3: `k` followed by `k` trigger positions `t` (strictly increasing). A trigger at `t` fires right after sample `t` (0-based) has been logged.

**Output**
- For each trigger: `trigger at t: s s s ...`, the frozen samples oldest first.

**Example**
```
Input:
5 40
100 101 102 ... 139   (the 40 values 100..139)
1 33

Output:
trigger at 33: 129 130 131 132 133
```
@@@ constraints_md
- Buffer length 32, `1 <= P <= 32`
- `1 <= n <= 100000`, `0 <= k <= n`, `0 <= t < n`
- `-32768 <= sample <= 32767`
@@@ starter_code
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdint.h>

#define BUF_LEN  32
#define MAX_IN   100000

static int16_t ring[BUF_LEN];   /* circular history                     */
static int     wr_idx;          /* next slot to write, 0..BUF_LEN-1     */
static int     stored;          /* samples held, saturates at BUF_LEN   */

static int16_t input[MAX_IN];
static int     trig_at[MAX_IN];

static void log_sample(int16_t s)
{
    ring[wr_idx] = s;
    wr_idx = (wr_idx + 1) % BUF_LEN;
    if (stored < BUF_LEN)
        stored++;
}

/* Copy the last 'pre' samples, oldest first, into out. Returns how many. */
static int snapshot(int16_t *out, int pre)
{
    if (pre > stored)
        pre = stored;
    int start = (wr_idx - pre) % BUF_LEN;          /* slot of the oldest sample wanted */
    for (int i = 0; i < pre; i++)
        out[i] = ring[(start + i) % BUF_LEN];
    return pre;
}

int main(void)
{
    int P, n, k;
    if (scanf("%d %d", &P, &n) != 2 || P < 1 || P > BUF_LEN || n < 1 || n > MAX_IN) return 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        int v;
        if (scanf("%d", &v) != 1) return 0;
        input[i] = (int16_t)v;
    }
    if (scanf("%d", &k) != 1 || k < 0 || k > n) return 0;
    for (int j = 0; j < k; j++)
        if (scanf("%d", &trig_at[j]) != 1) return 0;

    int next = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        log_sample(input[i]);
        if (next < k && trig_at[next] == i) {
            int16_t frozen[BUF_LEN];
            int cnt = snapshot(frozen, P);
            printf("trigger at %d:", i);
            for (int j = 0; j < cnt; j++) printf(" %d", frozen[j]);
            printf("\n");
            next++;
        }
    }
    return 0;
}
@@@ sample_input
4 6
1 2 3 4 5 6
2 2 5
@@@ sample_output
trigger at 2: 1 2 3
trigger at 5: 3 4 5 6

